  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "Whole protocomm security 2 exchanges as ESP-IDF's security2.c and protocomm.c make them, for the SRP case named by srpCase. Every message is a protobuf SessionData (session.proto: sec_ver = 2 as field 2, sec2 as field 12) holding a Sec2Payload (sec2.proto: msg as field 1, then sc0 20, sr0 21, sc1 22 or sr1 23), proto3, so a zero msg or status is left out. command0 (S2SessionCmd0: client_username 1, client_pubkey 2) and command1 (S2SessionCmd1: client_proof 1) are written to prov-session; response0 (S2SessionResp0: status 1, device_pubkey 2, device_salt 3) and response1 (S2SessionResp1: status 1, device_proof 2, device_nonce 3) are what a read of it then returns. nonce is response 1's device_nonce: the board's 8-byte session id, then a 32-bit big-endian counter of 1. After it, each setup message is sealed with AES-256-GCM under the first 32 bytes of K, no associated data, a 16-byte tag after the ciphertext. Both directions share the one counter, stepped after every message: the request to the board uses the counter, its answer the next. Requests go to hsn-setup; the answer is what a read returns.",
  "source": "ESP-IDF v6.1.1 (commit 051e4c4eb20346e043cdd47bc388fde75ff8af63): components/protocomm/src/security/security2.c, src/common/protocomm.c, src/crypto/srp6a/esp_srp.c and esp_srp_mpi.c, proto-c/*.pb-c.c; protobuf-c 1.4.1 (commit abc67a11c6db271bedbb9f58be85d6f4e2ea8389); Mbed TLS 4.1.1 with TF-PSA-Crypto (commit ce3f3485a121c100f58f36d700cb35b060f6e866). Compiled for the host and run by packages/protocol/src/pairing/esp-idf/make-vectors.sh",
